`eval.py` doesn't cover leave or announcements, so I tested those separately:
```
member before confirm: None
confirmed: True
member after confirm: <Member: e2ef16e8427@local.edu on reading-group@local.edu as MemberRole.member>
announcement delivered to subscriber: True
confirmed leave: True
member after leave: None
```

## Durability

This container has no init system (PID 1 is `sleep infinity`), so daemons don't come back on their own. I added `/usr/local/bin/start-mail-services.sh` (idempotent, regenerates the Postfix maps from current list state) plus a watchdog loop, and verified recovery by killing both daemons: both were back within 35 s.

Two things worth flagging:
- The `write`/`edit` tools are confined to the repo root, so system files were written via `bash`. All state is on disk at the paths above.
- I removed the throwaway accounts and subscriptions my testing created; the list is currently empty and ready for real subscribers.

